---
# Delivery alerts for the log collectors. Receipt at Alloy is not storage in
# Loki: these show when Alloy cannot hand lines to Loki, or drops them on
# purpose. Loki's own alerts are in the loki rule. TrueNASLogsSilent (no
# syslog from TrueNAS) must merge only after the first TrueNAS line has reached
# the receiver: until TrueNAS sends, the counter exists at 0 and the rule fires.
# Unit tests: scripts/validate-rules/alloy.test.yaml.
apiVersion: monitoring.coreos.com/v1
kind: PrometheusRule
metadata:
  name: alloy
  annotations:
    kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/substitute: disabled
spec:
  groups:
    - name: alloy
      rules:
        - alert: AlloyLinesRateLimited
          expr: sum by (component_id) (increase(loki_process_dropped_lines_total{reason="ratelimit_drop_stage"}[1h])) > 0
          labels:
            severity: warning
          annotations:
            summary: "Alloy dropped log lines in {{ $labels.component_id }}"
            description: "A source went over its line-rate cap. Lines dropped for being over the size limit or for coming from a sender that is not allowed are not counted; see loki_process_dropped_lines_total by reason. Expect this once after a TrueNAS reboot (boot burst) and when a new app runs its first backup; otherwise find the noisy source."
        - alert: AlloyWriteDropping
          expr: sum(increase(loki_write_dropped_entries_total[15m])) > 0
          labels:
            severity: warning
          annotations:
            summary: "Alloy gave up on log entries it could not send to Loki"
            description: "Loki was unreachable or refused them for longer than Alloy retries. The entries are lost (accepted: logs may be lost)."
        - alert: AlloyWriteRetrying
          expr: sum(rate(loki_write_batch_retries_total[10m])) > 0
          for: 15m
          labels:
            severity: warning
          annotations:
            summary: "Alloy keeps retrying pushes to Loki"
            description: "Loki is unreachable, slow, or answering 429 (the byte cap) or 5xx."
        - alert: SyslogParsingErrors
          expr: sum by (component_id) (increase(loki_source_syslog_parsing_errors_total[1h])) > 0
          labels:
            severity: warning
          annotations:
            summary: "Alloy cannot parse syslog messages in {{ $labels.component_id }}"
            description: "A sender uses another format or framing than the listener expects (TrueNAS: RFC 5424, octet counting; UCG: RFC 3164)."
        - alert: TrueNASLogsSilent
          expr: absent(loki_source_syslog_entries_total{component_id=~".*truenas.*"}) or sum(rate(loki_source_syslog_entries_total{component_id=~".*truenas.*"}[1h])) == 0
          for: 6h
          labels:
            severity: warning
          annotations:
            summary: "No syslog lines from TrueNAS for 6 hours"
            description: "The receiver got no line from TrueNAS (192.168.10.75, TCP 514) for 6 hours, or its counter is missing. Check that syslog-ng is active on TrueNAS and its syslog server is still 192.168.10.12 (TCP), and that alloy-receiver runs. A line from any other source address is dropped by the receiver's network policy without a count, so this alert is the only sign of it. Receipt is not storage: AlloyWriteDropping shows lines Alloy could not hand to Loki."
